{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNivUYvtm2HENfVX3fnje6","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map: KL Distillation for Sparse SwiGLU Activation Prediction\\\\n# Last updated: 2026-05-15\\\\n# Survey scope: 2023-2026, 4 directions\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# Direction 1: KL distillation for structured/activation sparsity\\\\n# Finding: NO prior work uses KL to train an activation sparsity PREDICTOR.\\\\n# Existing predictors use BCE (DejaVu, ShadowLLM). SPON uses KL but for\\\\n# learnable bias correction, not predictor training. This is our novelty.\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Resting Neurons, Active Insights: Robustify Activation Sparsity for Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Haotian Xu, Jiannan Yang, Tian Gao, Tsui-Wei Weng, Tengfei Ma]\\\\n  venue: ICML 2026\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2512.12744\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"最接近的KL蒸馏用于稀疏性的工作——但SPON训练的是可学习bias项而非predictor\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"SPON注入input-independent learnable activation vectors作为sparse computation的anchor，用KL散度(dense vs sparse logits)做distribution matching训练，训练后吸收进bias项，零推理开销\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"SPON证明KL divergence比BCE/MSE更适合sparsity场景的distribution matching。但SPON是全局bias correction而非per-token predictor——我们的predictor方案能实现input-dependent的sparsity pattern，比SPON更灵活。SPON在50-60% sparsity下测试，与我们目标一致\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Compact Language Models via Pruning and Knowledge Distillation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Saurav Muralidharan, Sharath Turuvekere Sreenivas, Raviraj Joshi, Marcin Chochowski, Mostofa Patwary, Mohammad Shoeybi, Bryan Catanzaro, Jan Kautz, Pavlo Molchanov]\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS 2024\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2407.14679\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"KL蒸馏用于结构化剪枝后恢复——验证logit-only KL优于intermediate matching\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"Minitron用logit-only forward KL divergence做structured pruning后的distillation recovery，发现仅用KL loss（不用CE或intermediate matching）效果最好，学生模型继承了teacher的inter-token关系和confidence calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"支持我们的核心假设：KL divergence保留output distribution比逐元素BCE更优。Minitron的发现（logit-only KL最优）为我们predictor的KL训练目标提供了理论支撑\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Instruction-Following Pruning for Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Bairu Hou, Qibin Chen, Jianyu Wang, Guoli Yin, Chong Wang, Nan Du, Ruoming Pang, Shiyu Chang, Tao Lei]\\\\n  venue: ICML 2025\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2501.02086\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"训练sparse mask predictor的范式——input-dependent mask selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"训练一个sparse mask predictor以instruction为输入动态选择最相关参数子集，联合优化mask predictor和LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"架构上与我们类似（训练predictor生成mask），但目标是instruction-aware weight pruning而非activation sparsity。可参考其predictor-LLM联合优化策略\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# Direction 2: Output distribution preservation in pruning/sparsity\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Distilling to Hybrid Attention Models via KL-Guided Layer Selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: []\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2512.20569\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"KL散度引导layer selection——用distribution差异决定哪些层需要保留\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"用KL divergence作为指标选择哪些attention层替换为hybrid attention，通过最小化output distribution变化来指导架构决策\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"方法论启示：KL divergence不仅可作为训练loss，还可作为layer-wise重要性指标。我们可用per-layer KL分析哪些层的sparsity对output distribution影响最大\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# Direction 3: SPON和类似的learnable bias correction for sparsity\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Fast Forward: Accelerating LLM Prefill with Predictive FFN Sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Aayush Gautam, Mukul Gagrani, Junyoung Park, Mingu Lee, Chiris Lott, Narasimha Reddy]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2602.00397\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Predictor + error compensation双组件架构——与SPON的bias correction思路互补\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"组合三个组件：(1) lightweight expert predictor选择high-importance neurons，(2) error compensation network修正sparsity误差，(3) layer-wise sparsity scheduler分配计算。50% FFN sparsity下达到1.45x prefill加速\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"与我们的方案最可比：都用predictor做activation sparsity。我们的差异在于用KL loss训练predictor而非BCE，且不需要额外的error compensation网络（KL loss本身应该能减少distribution shift）\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Amber Pruner: Leveraging N:M Activation Sparsity for Efficient Prefill in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Tai An, Ruwu Cai, Yanzhe Zhang, Yang Liu, Hao Chen, Pengcheng Xie, Sheng Chang, Yiwu Yao, Gongyi Wang]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2508.02128\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"N:M structured activation sparsity——hardware-friendly的sparsity pattern\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"Training-free的top-k策略在linear projection层内确定N:M activation masks，在2:4/4:8/8:16多种ratio下有效，可与W8A8量化组合\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"如果我们的predictor输出改为N:M structured pattern而非unstructured binary mask，可获得更好的hardware加速。值得作为future work\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# Direction 4: Predictor-based activation sparsity (TEAL, DejaVu, PowerInfer等)\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Training-Free Activation Sparsity in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [James Liu, Pragaash Ponnusamy, Tianle Cai, Han Guo, Yoon Kim, Ben Athiwaratkun]\\\\n  venue: ICLR 2025 (Spotlight)\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2408.14690\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"TEAL——我们的主要baseline，training-free magnitude pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"对所有hidden states施加magnitude-based sparsity（不需训练），在40-50% sparsity下性能降低很小，Llama-2/3和Mistral 7B-70B上验证。50% sparsity下1.8x decoding加速\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"TEAL用BCE度量sparsity mask质量（二元对错），我们的核心论点是：BCE只看neuron是否激活的对错，忽略了错误预测对output distribution的差异化影响。KL loss应该能让predictor学到'哪些neuron的错误预测对output影响更大'\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Deja Vu: Contextual Sparsity for Efficient LLMs at Inference Time\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Zichang Liu, Jue Wang, Tri Dao, Tianyi Zhou, Binhang Yuan, Zhao Song, Anshumali Shrivastava, Ce Zhang, Yuandong Tian, Christopher Re, Beidi Chen]\\\\n  venue: ICML 2023\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2310.17157\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Predictor-based contextual sparsity的开创性工作——我们的直接对比对象\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"用两层MLP predictor预测每层的contextual sparsity pattern（哪些attention heads和MLP neurons可跳过），在OPT-175B上实现2x加速。Predictor用BCE训练\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"DejaVu是predictor-based sparsity的baseline。其predictor用BCE训练——我们改用KL loss训练类似的predictor。关键差异：DejaVu在per-neuron level用BCE，我们在output distribution level用KL\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"ShadowLLM: Predictor-based Contextual Sparsity for Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Yash Akhauri, Ahmed F AbouElhamayed, Jordan Dotzel, Zhiru Zhang, Alexander M Rush, Safeen Huda, Mohamed S Abdelfattah]\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2024\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2406.16635\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DejaVu的改进——更好的predictor架构和sparsity pattern enforcement\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"Shadow predictor超越magnitude-based pruning，context-dependent评估attention head和neuron重要性。比DejaVu端到端精度提升15%，速度提升20%\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"ShadowLLM改进了predictor架构但仍用BCE-style loss。我们的改进方向正交：不改predictor架构，改训练loss（BCE→KL）。两种改进可能互补\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"SparseInfer: Training-free Prediction of Activation Sparsity for Fast LLM Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Jiho Shin, Hoeseok Yang, Youngmin Yi]\\\\n  venue: DATE 2025\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2411.12692\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Training-free sign-bit predictor——极低开销的sparsity预测\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"仅比较input和weight的sign bits预测activation sparsity，无需训练。仅适用于ReLU-based LLMs，不适用SwiGLU\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"不适用于SwiGLU模型（我们的目标），但其sign-bit方法的简洁性值得参考。SwiGLU缺乏天然sparsity证明trained predictor的必要性\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"SVD Contextual Sparsity Predictors for Fast LLM Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Georgii Serbin, Kirill Koshkin, Zhongao Sun, Anastasiya Bistrigova, C.C. Korikov]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2603.14110\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Training-free SVD-based sparsity predictor——用gate projection矩阵的SVD做预测\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"对ReGLU FFN的gate projection矩阵做truncation-aware SVD构建sparse pattern predictor，90% FFN sparsity下1.8x decoding加速，benchmark降低<1%\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"虽然是training-free competitor，但focus在ReGLU（不是SwiGLU）且需要90%天然稀疏性。我们的方法在SwiGLU的50%目标sparsity下工作，使用场景不同\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"CATS: Contextually-Aware Thresholding for Sparsity in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Donghyun Lee, Je-Yong Lee, Genghan Zhang, Mo Tiwari, Azalia Mirhoseini]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2404.08763\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Contextual thresholding——不训练predictor，用统计threshold做sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"为每个MLP层计算SiLU(x)激活的percentile threshold做sparsification，50% sparsity下性能降低1-2%，无需fine-tuning。Mistral-7B和Llama2-7B上验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"CATS直接在SwiGLU/SiLU模型上工作，是我们的直接competitor。但CATS是固定threshold不考虑input context，我们的trained predictor是input-dependent的，理论上更优\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"R-Sparse: Rank-Aware Activation Sparsity for Efficient LLM Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Zhenyu Zhang, Zechun Liu, Yuandong Tian, Harshit Khaitan, Zhangyang Wang, Steven Li]\\\\n  venue: ICLR 2025\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2504.19449\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Training-free rank-aware方法——利用input channel sparsity和SVD\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"用SVD分解将input channel sparsity映射到output，无需预测active channels。50% model-level sparsity下43%端到端加速\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"Training-free baseline。如果R-Sparse在SwiGLU模型上效果很好，我们需要证明trained KL predictor的额外训练成本是值得的\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Efficient LLM Inference using Dynamic Input Pruning and Cache-Aware Masking\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Marco Federici, Davide Belli, Mart van Baalen, Amir Jalalirad, Andrii Skliar, Bence Major, Markus Nagel, Paul Whatmough]\\\\n  venue: MLSys 2025\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2412.01380\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Predictor-free dynamic pruning for SwiGLU——直接针对SwiGLU的magnitude pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"Predictor-free方案动态剪枝SwiGLU MLP层，配合LoRA adapter恢复精度。Phi-3-Medium上46%内存减少+40%吞吐提升\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"直接针对SwiGLU的competitor。DIP证明SwiGLU的sparsity pattern难以预测（所以放弃predictor），我们的KL-trained predictor需要证明能克服这个挑战\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# 补充：Activation function替换和sparsity增强\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"ReLU Strikes Back: Exploiting Activation Sparsity in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Iman Mirzadeh, Keivan Alizadeh, Sachin Mehta, Carlo C Del Mundo, Oncel Tuzel, Golnoosh Samei, Mohammad Rastegari, Mehrdad Farajtabar]\\\\n  venue: ICLR 2024\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2310.04564\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"ReLU替换SiLU获得天然sparsity——替代路线\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"用ReLU替换SiLU/GELU后continual pretraining，获得天然高稀疏性（>90%），推理计算减少3x\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"替代路线：修改activation function vs 训练predictor。我们的定位：不需要修改pretrained模型架构，作为plug-in predictor在现有SwiGLU模型上工作\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Turbo Sparse: Achieving LLM SOTA Performance with Minimal Activated Parameters\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Yixin Song, Haotong Xie, Zhengyan Zhang, Bo Wen, Li Ma, Zeyu Mi, Haibo Chen]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2406.05955\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"dReLU获得90%+ sparsity——activation function工程的极致\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"提出dReLU使LLM达到近90% sparsity同时保持SOTA性能，2-5x decoding加速\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"与ReLU Strikes Back同一思路但更极端。我们不改activation function，这是差异化定位\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"ProSparse: Introducing and Enhancing Intrinsic Activation Sparsity within Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Chenyang Song, Xu Han, Zhengyan Zhang, Shengding Hu, Xiyu Shi, Kuai Li, Chen Chen, Zhiyuan Liu, Guangli Li, Tao Yang, Maosong Sun]\\\\n  venue: COLING 2025\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2402.13516\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Progressive sparsification——渐进式增加sparsity regularization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"三步法：ReLU替换→progressive sparsity regularization（沿sine curve增强）→threshold shifting(FATReLU)。LLaMA2-7B达89.32% sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"ProSparse的progressive training策略可参考：我们的KL predictor训练也可渐进式增加sparsity目标（已在Lagrangian约束中实现）\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"Sparsing Law: Towards Large Language Models with Greater Activation Sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Yuqi Luo, Chenyang Song, Xu Han, Yingfa Chen, Chaojun Xiao, Xiaojun Meng, Liqun Deng, Jiansheng Wei, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun]\\\\n  venue: arXiv\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2411.02335\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Activation sparsity的scaling law——理论基础\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"SiLU/SwiGLU的activation ratio随训练递增（变密），ReLU递减（变稀）。Sparsity对parameter scale不敏感，与width-depth ratio线性相关\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"理论支撑：SiLU/SwiGLU模型天然不够稀疏（随训练变密），因此需要外部predictor/pruning来获得稀疏性——这是我们工作的motivation之一\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- title: \\\\\\\"A Sparsity Predicting Approach for Large Language Models via Activation Pattern Clustering\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nobel Dhar, Bobin Deng, Md Romyull Islam, Xinyue Zhang, Kazi Fahim Ahmad Nasif, Kun Suo]\\\\n  venue: Euro-Par 2025\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2507.14179\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Clustering-based sparsity prediction——用聚类简化prediction\\\\\\\"\\\\n  key_finding: \\\\\\\"将activation patterns聚类为representative clusters，预测cluster assignment而非individual neuron states，减少prediction开销。Mistral-7B上79.34%聚类精度\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"降低predictor复杂度的思路。如果我们的per-neuron KL predictor开销太大，可考虑cluster-level prediction\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n# 竞争格局总结\\\\n# =============================================================================\\\\n#\\\\n# 我们的独特定位:\\\\n# 1. 唯一使用KL divergence训练activation sparsity predictor的工作\\\\n#    - DejaVu/ShadowLLM用BCE训练predictor\\\\n#    - SPON用KL但训练bias correction而非predictor\\\\n#    - TEAL/CATS/R-Sparse/SparseInfer/SVD-CSP是training-free\\\\n# 2. 专注SwiGLU模型的50% sparsity目标\\\\n#    - ReLU/dReLU方案需要替换activation function\\\\n#    - 很多training-free方案在SwiGLU上效果不佳(DIP论文证实)\\\\n# 3. 通过保留output distribution(而非逐neuron匹配)来指导sparsity\\\\n#    - Minitron/SPON已证明KL loss优于MSE/BCE做distribution matching\\\\n#    - 我们将此insight应用到predictor训练\\\\n#\\\\n# 主要related work定位:\\\\n# - vs TEAL: trained predictor(input-dependent) vs fixed magnitude threshold\\\\n# - vs DejaVu/ShadowLLM: KL loss vs BCE loss训练predictor\\\\n# - vs SPON: predictor vs learnable bias; 都用KL但目标不同\\\\n# - vs DIP: trained predictor vs predictor-free pruning\\\\n# - vs ReLU/TurboSparse/ProSparse: 不改activation function\\\\n# - vs Fast Forward: KL loss vs BCE+error compensation\\\\n# - vs CATS: input-dependent predictor vs fixed percentile threshold\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 13950, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017vjbXYVvyJXnJdrHHVpJQT","session_id":"be4af677-c918-498a-8593-19b0dadd846b","uuid":"0c651a0a-68fe-44f2-ad5a-1b9347aa3801","timestamp":"2026-05-15T17:40:34.342Z"}
